sid='1PFPcRXVh1pSjdnhRDroQIx_IvBESy4EV';raw,pages=b.source(sid);text='\n'.join(pages[:2]);text=text[text.index('The world’s'):];parts=split(text,['The world’s','These transition','This degradation','Desertification does','Desertification became','Increased population','It is a common','While desertification','In the last'])
parts[0]='The world’s great deserts were formed by natural processes interacting over long intervals of time. During most of these times, deserts have grown and shrunk independently of human activities. Paleodeserts (large sand seas now inactive because they are stabilized by vegetation) extend well beyond the present margins of core deserts, such as the Sahara. In some regions, deserts are separated sharply from surrounding, less arid, areas by mountains and other contrasting landforms that reflect basic structural differences in the regional geology. In other areas, desert fringes form a gradual transition from a dry to a more humid environment, making it more difficult to define the desert border.'
parts[4]='Desertification became well known in the 1930s, when parts of the Great Plains in the United States turned into the ‘dust bowl’ as a result of drought and poor practices in farming, although the term itself was not used until almost 1950. During the dust bowl period, millions of people were forced to abandon their farms and livelihoods. Greatly improved methods of agriculture and land and water management in the Great Plains have prevented that disaster from recurring, but desertification presently affects millions of people in almost every continent.'
paras=[{'label':chr(65+i),'text':re.sub(r'\s+[BcDE]\s*$','',t)} for i,t in enumerate(parts)]
iq=['a description of how deserts move across the land in an irregular way','an account of how productive land was turned into desert in the early twentieth century','the effects of migration on the desertification process','a description of a method for tracking desertification','a description of different types of deserts','reference to a lack of agreement between scientists on how deserts form','an example of the fatal effects of poor farming practices']
tq=['In some areas it is difficult to see where a desert begins.','Soil erosion is increased because of the impact of farm animals.','The most common cause of desertification is a lack of rain.','West Africa has yet to recover from the 1968 drought.','The press are uninterested in the problem of desertification.','Technology that can help to show the relationship between humans, livestock and desertification has yet to be invented.']
